1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,480
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,050
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:06,120
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,950
I've laid brick for
forty-one years.

5
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:10,790
Most of that on my knees,

6
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:12,220
laying the bottom courses,

7
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,780
one brick at a time.

8
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:14,870
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,280
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,750
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:20,110
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,290
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:23,370
and it went away.

14
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:24,860
This is different.

15
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,500
Tight.

16
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:25,850
Full.

17
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:26,800
Like a band around

18
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,390
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:29,690
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,010
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,180
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:34,550
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:35,850
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,200
At three months,

25
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,080
give it six.

26
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,270
At six months,

27
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:40,760
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:41,740
At a year,

29
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:43,390
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,360
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,400
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,870
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,110
Every session,

34
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:49,740
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,070
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,670
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,130
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:55,540
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:57,520
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,750
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:00,010
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:01,280
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,120
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:04,610
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:05,690
operation to go back

46
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:06,770
in and do it over.

47
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:07,840
I said no.

48
00:01:08,070 --> 00:01:09,280
Every morning I climbed
out

49
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:10,610
of the truck at the job

50
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:11,450
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:13,060
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,090
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,380
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:17,890
for it and picked up my
trowel.

55
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:20,500
Couldn't kneel to lay a
bottom course,

56
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,220
couldn't climb the
scaffold without

57
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:23,910
stopping on every landing,

58
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:25,260
couldn't carry a load of
brick up

59
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,150
the ramp without favoring
that leg.

60
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:28,860
The young guys on my crew
started

61
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,540
laying my low courses for
me.

62
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:32,060
Nobody said anything.

63
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,370
They didn't have to.

64
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:35,260
A bricklayer who can't get
down

65
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:36,560
on his knees is a
bricklayer

66
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,670
running out of time.

67
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,150
It woke me at night,

68
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:40,710
and it turned ordinary
things,

69
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:41,700
like getting in the truck

70
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,080
or up off a bucket,

71
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,170
into a decision.

72
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,060
After a long and serious

73
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,050
talk with my wife,

74
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:48,770
I went back in one more
time.

75
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,100
That was the fourth set

76
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,680
of X-rays on this knee.

77
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,600
And like the three before
it,

78
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,150
the answer was everything
looks great.

79
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:58,130
No loosening, no
infection,

80
00:01:58,130 --> 00:01:59,130
nothing wrong.

81
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,360
Only this time there

82
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:01,550
was no new number.

83
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:04,140
Nobody said give it
another six months.

84
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,070
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,410
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:08,520
lot for a while.

87
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,700
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:11,060
Then explain this.

89
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,340
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:14,800
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:17,180
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

92
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:19,230
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:19,230 --> 00:02:20,950
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

94
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:22,060
with my leg up,

95
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:23,780
trying to find any angle
where

96
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,370
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

97
00:02:25,370 --> 00:02:26,820
around my knee and
tightening.

98
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:27,920
I had a wall

99
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,010
to start at seven.

100
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,570
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:33,960
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:34,920
And I just thought,

103
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,570
is this really how it
ends?

104
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:37,970
Forty-one years,

105
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:39,210
and I hang up the trowel

106
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:40,380
because of a knee that
looks

107
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,750
great on an X-ray?

108
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,780
So I made myself a
promise.

109
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:45,010
I wouldn't go a day

110
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:46,580
without looking for an
answer.

111
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,430
And when I found one,

112
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:49,780
I'd share it with everyone

113
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,280
going through the same
thing.

114
00:02:51,510 --> 00:02:52,620
So I got my laptop

115
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:53,970
out and went looking.

116
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:55,700
Not for a product.

117
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:57,000
For an explanation.

118
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,890
Mayo Clinic forums,

119
00:02:58,890 --> 00:03:01,070
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

120
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:03,740
doctor videos, medical
animations.

121
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:05,550
And that's when I found a
video

122
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:07,190
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

123
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:08,520
Steven Salinger,

124
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,750
whose own wife had been

125
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:11,440
through exactly this.

126
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,850
But before I say anything
else,

127
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:15,310
I want to be straight with
you.

128
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:17,870
You've already had
something work fast.

129
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:18,900
The ice.

130
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,750
The first week of a new
pill.

131
00:03:20,810 --> 00:03:22,530
The good day after a
session.

132
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:23,890
Then it wore off.

133
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:26,320
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

134
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,520
Fast relief isn't relief.

135
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,740
It's a preview.

136
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:31,090
So I'm not going to tell

137
00:03:31,090 --> 00:03:32,970
you this works fast.

138
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:33,860
It doesn't.

139
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,910
But if you're willing to
be patient,

140
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:36,840
and to look at what's

141
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,800
going on around your new
knee

142
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,180
instead of inside it,

143
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,830
there is a real reason

144
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:43,050
it still hurts.

145
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:45,160
And something you can do
about it.

146
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,650
Let me explain what he
said,

147
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:48,310
because this is what
changed

148
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:49,580
everything for me.

149
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,320
He started with the
basics.

150
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,840
A knee replacement takes
out

151
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,560
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

152
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,620
in metal and plastic.

153
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:57,840
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

154
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,380
you had before the
operation.

155
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,190
That part I already knew.

156
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:02,900
But then he explained
something

157
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,320
nobody had ever told me.

158
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:05,260
He said,

159
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,680
think about a swollen foot

160
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,730
inside a shoe.

161
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:09,240
The shoe didn't shrink.

162
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:11,340
Your foot is taking up
more room,

163
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:12,820
so everything feels
cramped

164
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:14,320
and tight and squeezed.

165
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:15,580
Your new knee sits

166
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,030
in a limited space

167
00:04:17,030 --> 00:04:18,450
with living tissue

168
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:19,690
packed all around it.

169
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,800
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

170
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,620
had to work through that
tissue.

171
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,550
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

172
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:28,530
At first that's normal.

173
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:30,700
But in some people that
swelling can

174
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:33,690
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

175
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:35,460
And swollen tissue takes
up more

176
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,280
room than calm tissue
does.

177
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,450
So when you bend,

178
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:40,430
that tissue gets
compressed.

179
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,790
When you straighten,

180
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:42,950
it gets pulled tight.

181
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:43,760
That's the band.

182
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,920
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

183
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:46,810
And you start being

184
00:04:46,810 --> 00:04:47,800
the one who says,

185
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,490
you go ahead.

186
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:49,530
I'll stay here.

187
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,440
And that's exactly why so
much

188
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,220
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

189
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,400
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

190
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,310
around the knee.

191
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:57,840
Worth doing,

192
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,770
and I'd done it.

193
00:04:58,810 --> 00:05:00,270
It does nothing about
tissue

194
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:01,360
taking up room.

195
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:02,570
A nerve block quiets

196
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:04,180
the nerve carrying the
signal.

197
00:05:04,370 --> 00:05:06,780
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

198
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,640
But when that irritated
tissue

199
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:10,230
finally calms down,

200
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,850
it holds less fluid,

201
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:13,470
and it takes up less room.

202
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,100
Less room taken up means

203
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,130
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

204
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,930
That's what takes the
pressure off.

205
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,770
After two years of this,

206
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:22,350
it finally made sense.

207
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:24,700
The problem was never the
new knee.

208
00:05:24,910 --> 00:05:26,750
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

209
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,530
He calls it the squeeze.

210
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,990
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

211
00:05:31,170 --> 00:05:33,000
I'd bought gel knee pads,

212
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,710
a foam kneeling board,

213
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:37,030
compression braces,
creams,

214
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:38,720
half of Amazon really,

215
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,070
and all any of it gave

216
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:41,480
me was an hour.

217
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,640
I even looked at going

218
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:44,500
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

219
00:05:44,690 --> 00:05:46,880
But at $200 a session

220
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,240
with nothing covered by
insurance,

221
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,640
that was a quick no.

222
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:52,380
Then one night I went

223
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,680
back to that knee
replacement

224
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,030
group and actually read
it.

225
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:56,730
Thousands of people,

226
00:05:56,730 --> 00:05:58,330
years out from surgery,

227
00:05:58,330 --> 00:06:00,860
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

228
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,250
nobody could explain.

229
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:04,350
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

230
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:06,120
the same thing kept coming
up.

231
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:08,060
This one device,

232
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,380
and people saying

233
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,320
it was the first thing

234
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,530
that made a difference.

235
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,740
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

236
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,200
alright, here it comes,

237
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,650
he's selling me something,

238
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:18,380
let me shut that down
right now.

239
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,440
I'm only here because I
made myself

240
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,610
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

241
00:06:22,610 --> 00:06:23,690
that if I ever found

242
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:24,940
something that helped,

243
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:26,000
I'd say so.

244
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,170
It's called the KenRelief

245
00:06:28,170 --> 00:06:29,990
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

246
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:32,190
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

247
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:34,180
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

248
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:36,400
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

249
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,140
But I went to their
website anyway,

250
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:39,000
just to see what all

251
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,030
the fuss was about.

252
00:06:40,250 --> 00:06:43,100
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

253
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,330
charge $200 a session

254
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:47,050
for, off machines that
cost

255
00:06:47,050 --> 00:06:48,720
fifty thousand dollars,

256
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,730
in a wrap you plug

257
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:50,930
into the wall at home.

258
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,940
Two hundred and forty
lights.

259
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:55,750
Red at 660 nanometers

260
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,310
and near-infrared at 850,

261
00:06:58,310 --> 00:07:00,490
run together for the
strongest effect.

262
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,560
Four strength levels.

263
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,710
A five to thirty minute
timer.

264
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:06,850
Then I saw the guarantee.

265
00:07:06,890 --> 00:07:08,120
Ninety days.

266
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,020
Results or your money
back,

267
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:12,140
no questions, no store
credit,

268
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,740
and you don't even send it
back.

269
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:16,630
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

270
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:18,230
days to change my mind.

271
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:19,640
There wasn't much to lose,

272
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:20,630
so I ordered it.

273
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:22,040
Two of them, actually.

274
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:24,560
Only the right knee was
replaced,

275
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,780
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

276
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,060
and I'd done it on every

277
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,680
job for two years.

278
00:07:30,130 --> 00:07:31,330
The left one

279
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:32,900
was carrying the
difference.

280
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,130
When it came,

281
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:36,930
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

282
00:07:36,930 --> 00:07:38,170
because I'd been let down
too

283
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:39,760
many times to get excited.

284
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:41,550
What I felt was warmth.

285
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:43,480
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

286
00:07:43,850 --> 00:07:45,360
More like it was coming
from inside

287
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,870
the knee and spreading
around it.

288
00:07:47,030 --> 00:07:48,210
And that was it.

289
00:07:48,370 --> 00:07:50,110
That was the whole
experience.

290
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:51,720
When I took it off,

291
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,630
I'll be honest,

292
00:07:52,630 --> 00:07:54,350
nothing dramatic had
happened.

293
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,150
And after what that video
said,

294
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:58,330
that's exactly what I
expected.

295
00:07:58,630 --> 00:07:59,780
What was different

296
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:00,830
was that for the first

297
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,310
time in two years

298
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:04,130
I'd done something for my
knee

299
00:08:04,130 --> 00:08:05,150
instead of to it.

300
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:06,210
Twenty minutes,

301
00:08:06,210 --> 00:08:07,120
in my own chair,

302
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,110
after work.

303
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,240
No drive, no copay.

304
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:12,010
They say twenty minutes.

305
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:12,880
I did thirty,

306
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:14,180
twice a day,

307
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:16,550
lowest setting that first
week.

308
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:18,370
Once before the truck in
the morning,

309
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:19,610
once after supper.

310
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:20,530
The first week,

311
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:21,360
I couldn't have told

312
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,900
you if anything was
happening.

313
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:24,150
I tried not to get

314
00:08:24,150 --> 00:08:24,980
my hopes up.

315
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:26,110
I'd had things help

316
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:27,580
for a week and then stop.

317
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:29,190
But somewhere in the
second week

318
00:08:29,190 --> 00:08:30,300
I noticed I'd come down

319
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,010
the stairs without holding
the rail.

320
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,600
I hadn't decided to.

321
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,680
I just did it,

322
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,960
then stopped halfway down
because I realized.

323
00:08:37,210 --> 00:08:38,040
By the end of the fourth

324
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,060
week I'd slept through

325
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,830
the night four times
running.

326
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,690
I stood at the counter and
finished

327
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:44,910
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

328
00:08:45,230 --> 00:08:46,660
None of that is dramatic.

329
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:47,780
All of it was gone

330
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:48,910
for two years.

331
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,760
A few weeks later my wife
asked

332
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,580
if I wanted to walk

333
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:53,230
the long way around the
block.

334
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,500
And for the first time

335
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,320
in two years,

336
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,500
I said yes.

337
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,150
I wanted to understand
why,

338
00:08:58,150 --> 00:08:59,460
so I read the whole thing.

339
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:01,540
It comes down to four
steps.

340
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:02,420
One.

341
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,930
The tissue around a new
knee

342
00:09:04,930 --> 00:09:06,420
can stay inflamed long
after

343
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,560
surgery is over.

344
00:09:07,930 --> 00:09:08,460
Two.

345
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,860
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

346
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:11,780
so it takes up more

347
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:12,930
room than it should.

348
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:13,730
Three.

349
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:15,990
There's only so much room
in there.

350
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,580
Bending compresses it.

351
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,440
Straightening pulls it
tight.

352
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,870
That's the squeeze.

353
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:21,740
Four.

354
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:23,710
Red and near-infrared
light have been

355
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:25,490
studied for calming that
inflammation,

356
00:09:25,490 --> 00:09:26,800
so the swelling and the
pressure

357
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:27,970
can come down with it.

358
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,620
In a randomized trial,

359
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:31,620
patients given light
therapy after

360
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:32,830
a knee replacement

361
00:09:32,830 --> 00:09:34,040
had less pain,

362
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,880
less swelling and better
early

363
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:37,520
movement than those who
weren't.

364
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:40,380
A 2025 review said the
same,

365
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:41,680
and was clear the evidence

366
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,830
is still limited.

367
00:09:42,970 --> 00:09:44,720
I probably sound like a
broken record

368
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,180
to my family and my crew.

369
00:09:46,770 --> 00:09:48,610
But after two years of
doing everything

370
00:09:48,610 --> 00:09:50,550
I was told and getting
nowhere,

371
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:51,950
you have no idea what it's

372
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:53,690
like to sleep through the
night,

373
00:09:53,690 --> 00:09:54,880
say yes to the walk,

374
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,310
and get my life back.

375
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,690
So take it from me.

376
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,650
Don't spend another year
waiting

377
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:00,700
for it to settle.

378
00:10:00,950 --> 00:10:02,820
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

379
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:04,480
More than ten thousand
people

380
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,630
with pain after a knee

381
00:10:05,630 --> 00:10:08,150
replacement have already
tried this.

382
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:10,100
Some had it worse than I
did.

383
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:11,490
You can get the KenRelief

384
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:13,090
wrap from their website,

385
00:10:13,090 --> 00:10:14,880
with a discount link and
ninety

386
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:16,000
days to try it.

387
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,820
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

388
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:20,000
you get your money back

389
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,310
and you keep the wrap.

390
00:10:21,610 --> 00:10:23,270
They only release so many

391
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:24,500
at that price.

392
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:25,820
If it's still there,

393
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:26,980
get one,

394
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,626
and stop the squeeze.

